 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "The playlist has numSongs songs numbered 1..numSongs. Shuffle Mode plays the songs in cycles: each cycle plays every song exactly once in some order, then a new cycle begins. sequence is a window of observed plays that may start and end in the middle of a cycle. Return true when there is an offset o (0 <= o < numSongs) such that cutting sequence before positions o, o + numSongs, o + 2 * numSongs, ... gives pieces in which no song repeats (a full piece of numSongs distinct songs is a whole cycle; the first and last pieces are partial cycles). Otherwise return false. An empty sequence returns true.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk09-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
